WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.534
-Welcome to the show. -Thank you.

00:00:02.534 --> 00:00:04.167
-I'm so happy to have you on. I'm a big fan.

00:00:04.167 --> 00:00:05.334
-Thank you. -You look great.

00:00:05.334 --> 00:00:07.467
Am I saying your name correct?

00:00:07.467 --> 00:00:08.968
Is it Camille Cottin? [cotton]

00:00:08.968 --> 00:00:10.968
-Again? No, I'm kidding.

00:00:10.968 --> 00:00:13.567
-Camille Cottin in America. -Yeah, yeah. It's perfect.

00:00:13.567 --> 00:00:16.100
Yeah, it twists. It's great. Yeah.

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:19.133
-In France -- -It's flat.

00:00:19.133 --> 00:00:21.634
It's like Camille Coh-tawn. So I prefer the way you said it.

00:00:21.634 --> 00:00:23.734
-Ooh. Really, I thought that was beautiful what you said.

00:00:23.734 --> 00:00:25.267
-Oh, yeah? -Camille Coh-tawn.

00:00:25.267 --> 00:00:26.801
-Flat. Yeah, that's it.

00:00:26.801 --> 00:00:28.367
-I almost want to whisper your name.

00:00:28.367 --> 00:00:30.367
-Again? -Camille Coh-tawn.

00:00:30.367 --> 00:00:33.734
-Yes. Yes, Jimmy, yes.

00:00:33.734 --> 00:00:36.400
Jimmy Fal-ohn. -Ooh, I like that a lot.

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:37.601
[ Audience oohs ]

00:00:37.601 --> 00:00:40.000
That's got a good ring to it.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:41.434
You have a lot of fans here

00:00:41.434 --> 00:00:44.634
because of the show "Call My Agent."

00:00:44.634 --> 00:00:48.400
It's a French show that just kind of exploded in the U.S.

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:50.033
when it came to Netflix,

00:00:50.033 --> 00:00:52.567
and they just announced you're doing another season.

00:00:52.567 --> 00:00:55.367
-Are we? -Yeah. Yeah.

00:00:55.367 --> 00:00:56.834
Just now. I just heard right before the show.

00:00:56.834 --> 00:00:58.734
Congratulations. -Well, thanks.

00:00:58.734 --> 00:00:59.968
[ Cheers and applause ] Thanks. Cool.

00:00:59.968 --> 00:01:02.000
-How does it feel, though, when you find out

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:04.000
that people are loving it over here.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:05.367
Is it fun?

00:01:05.367 --> 00:01:09.200
-Well, I'm just starting to realize it, I have to say.

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:11.801
-Oh, really? -Yeah, well, being invited

00:01:11.801 --> 00:01:13.667
by you, it's like -- Oh, yeah, this is serious.

00:01:13.667 --> 00:01:15.400
-Oh, yeah. Yeah.

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:19.000
-But it's very recent. Yeah. We didn't know.

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:21.234
We wrapped, and then there was the pandemic.

00:01:21.234 --> 00:01:23.667
And then suddenly it's like, "America loves you!"

00:01:23.667 --> 00:01:26.968
And you're like, "What?" I mean, America --

00:01:26.968 --> 00:01:29.033
I just went to the supermarket this afternoon,

00:01:29.033 --> 00:01:30.868
and they were really normal with me,

00:01:30.868 --> 00:01:32.434
so I think it's still a niche.

00:01:32.434 --> 00:01:34.200
-No. No. People know.

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:36.434
I mean, now you're doing these giant movies, too.

00:01:36.434 --> 00:01:37.868
You're working with --

00:01:37.868 --> 00:01:42.167
You were in "House of Gucci" with our pal Lady "Ga-ga."

00:01:42.167 --> 00:01:46.133
We love her. Did you get to hang out with Lady Gaga?

00:01:46.133 --> 00:01:49.100
-Oh, I wish I could, but she was really concentrating.

00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:51.300
So she was into her character.

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:52.934
-You're supposed to be enemies in the movie.

00:01:52.934 --> 00:01:54.067
-Yeah. Yeah, I'm her rival.

00:01:54.067 --> 00:01:55.667
I'm stealing her husband,

00:01:55.667 --> 00:01:57.133
so obviously she doesn't really like me.

00:01:57.133 --> 00:01:59.734
-Yeah. She has a point. -She has a point.

00:01:59.734 --> 00:02:01.267
But I have to say

00:02:01.267 --> 00:02:03.501
that she's really not like her character in life.

00:02:03.501 --> 00:02:06.701
So she was really concentrated, and then suddenly

00:02:06.701 --> 00:02:09.400
she came between two takes and she said,

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:11.567
"You're a beautiful woman. You're a lovely actress.

00:02:11.567 --> 00:02:13.734
And at the end of the movie, we'll be friends. Now hush!"

00:02:13.734 --> 00:02:16.000
[ Laughter ]

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:18.934
-That's -- We love you, Gaga. Exactly right.

00:02:18.934 --> 00:02:20.767
"At the end of the movie, we'll be friends," yeah.

00:02:20.767 --> 00:02:22.167
-Yeah, she was nice.

00:02:22.167 --> 00:02:25.133
-You've been performing since you were a child.

00:02:25.133 --> 00:02:28.033
And you actually -- Your mom started a theater club?

00:02:28.033 --> 00:02:30.100
-Oh, yeah. Yeah.

00:02:30.100 --> 00:02:32.734
-What was it like working for your mom?

00:02:32.734 --> 00:02:35.934
-Right. So, yeah. She created a theater club.

00:02:35.934 --> 00:02:38.934
She had never acted, but she decided she would do this.

00:02:38.934 --> 00:02:43.000
And then she decided that she would create this --

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:45.200
It's a bit like "Troy," the movie with Brad Pitt.

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:47.400
-Yes. -So it's a French play.

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:50.634
And I was given the part of Helene,

00:02:50.634 --> 00:02:52.300
the most beautiful woman of the world.

00:02:52.300 --> 00:02:54.534
It's obviously it's because my mom was giving the parts.

00:02:54.534 --> 00:02:55.901
-Casting, yeah. She's like, "I know who

00:02:55.901 --> 00:02:57.634
the most beautiful girl is. My daughter!"

00:02:57.634 --> 00:03:00.100
-"Yeah, I got the part!"

00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:02.701
And then, yeah, it was just incredible

00:03:02.701 --> 00:03:05.567
because the most handsome guy of the school

00:03:05.567 --> 00:03:07.534
just went to the theater club,

00:03:07.534 --> 00:03:10.300
which is unusual because normally you get the geek guys.

00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:12.367
-Yeah. Of course. The jock or...

00:03:12.367 --> 00:03:14.033
-Yeah, yeah, not the cool guys.

00:03:14.033 --> 00:03:17.767
And he was to be my lover in the play.

00:03:17.767 --> 00:03:19.968
So I was, like, "Well, thank you, Mommy.

00:03:19.968 --> 00:03:22.033
My dream is coming true."

00:03:22.033 --> 00:03:23.534
-Best mom ever!

00:03:23.534 --> 00:03:25.534
-But until then, it was all great.

00:03:25.534 --> 00:03:27.467
And then we had to perform,

00:03:27.467 --> 00:03:30.767
and he quit, like, I don't know, a week before.

00:03:30.767 --> 00:03:33.367
So she said, "Now we'll never find somebody to do it.

00:03:33.367 --> 00:03:35.434
So I'll do it."

00:03:35.434 --> 00:03:37.067
[ Laughter ]

00:03:37.067 --> 00:03:38.234
-Mom? -Mom.

00:03:38.234 --> 00:03:39.734
Mom was on stage with me.

00:03:39.734 --> 00:03:42.501
-So Mom stepped in for him? -Yeah.

00:03:42.501 --> 00:03:45.834
And she was like, "My Princess, come and give me a kiss."

00:03:45.834 --> 00:03:47.100
And it was like...

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:48.868
[ Laughter ]

00:03:48.868 --> 00:03:52.467
-Oh, I love that. That's a pro right there.

00:03:52.467 --> 00:03:55.734
That's a pro move right there, Mom. Good job.

00:03:55.734 --> 00:03:57.601
Let's talk about "Killing Eve."

00:03:57.601 --> 00:03:59.734
It's the fourth and the final season.

00:03:59.734 --> 00:04:01.834
-Yes. -And what -- Can you --

00:04:01.834 --> 00:04:03.901
Can you set up what's happening with your character?

00:04:03.901 --> 00:04:07.334
-Oh, Helene. She's a villain. She's a true villain.

00:04:07.334 --> 00:04:08.601
-Yes. -Vill-Helene. Yeah.

00:04:08.601 --> 00:04:11.434
And what am I allowed to say? I don't know.

00:04:11.434 --> 00:04:13.467
-I don't really know, either, because you're not really

00:04:13.467 --> 00:04:14.934
allowed to spoil -- -No, not really.

00:04:14.934 --> 00:04:17.667
-No. So, she's a villain.

00:04:17.667 --> 00:04:19.400
-Yeah. She's a villain.

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:20.834
-That's all you can say.

00:04:20.834 --> 00:04:22.834
-She's a very, very villain villain.

00:04:22.834 --> 00:04:25.133
-Wow. A double villain? -No.

00:04:25.133 --> 00:04:28.300
Yeah, double villain. -That's a spoiler. Okay.

00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:30.067
-No. I can say she's a mom. -Yeah.

00:04:30.067 --> 00:04:31.667
-And I thought it was quite funny

00:04:31.667 --> 00:04:34.267
to be a villain and to be a mom. -Yeah.

00:04:34.267 --> 00:04:36.200
-No, but I think it's -- Yeah, an interesting character.

00:04:36.200 --> 00:04:38.834
-It's great. And congrats. It's another hit.

00:04:38.834 --> 00:04:40.667
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:04:40.667 --> 00:04:43.767
Here's Camille Coh-tawn...

00:04:43.767 --> 00:04:45.067
in "Killing Eve."

00:04:45.067 --> 00:04:46.267
Take a look at this.

00:04:47.467 --> 00:04:49.400
-Ow! -I feel rude you cooking me

00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:52.300
dinner when I hardly know anything about you.

00:04:52.300 --> 00:04:54.100
Tell me about yourself.

00:04:54.100 --> 00:04:59.000
-I like holidays, dogs, long walks on the beach.

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:01.934
-And?

00:05:01.934 --> 00:05:04.133
-And I want to bring down the 12.

00:05:04.133 --> 00:05:05.968
I want to cut the head off the monster.

00:05:05.968 --> 00:05:09.734
-That's wonderful. I like all of those things, too.

00:05:11.067 --> 00:05:12.634
And guess what.

00:05:12.634 --> 00:05:16.067
I also want to get the head of the monster.

00:05:16.067 --> 00:05:18.267
-Really? -Amazing, isn't it,

00:05:18.267 --> 00:05:20.968
when you find someone you can really connect with?

00:05:20.968 --> 00:05:23.267
-That's right. That's how you do it.

00:05:23.267 --> 00:05:25.100
Camille Cottin.

00:05:25.100 --> 00:05:29.467
"Killing Eve" airs Sundays on BBC America and AMC Plus.

